  "raw": {
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17115": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Doctoral Studies",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Doctoral Studies Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Doctoral Studies Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F270069P Open Date 09/24/2026 Close Date Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor of Doctoral Studies Salary $71,000 Assistant Professor; $75,000 Associate Professor Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Is Tenured/ Tenure Track Yes Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Job Description Summary The Educational Leadership program at Chicago State University invites applications from well-qualified candidates to fill a tenure-track faculty position beginning September 1st, 2026. The selected individual will teach Educational Leadership courses in Doctoral Studies, PreK-12 School Leadership, Higher Education Administration, and Instructional Leadership. Required Education Qualified applicants should possess a terminal degree (Ph.D., Ed.D.) in Educational Leadership or related field. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Preference will be given to candidates who have an earned doctoral degree in Educational Leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Preferred Qualifications 1) Current and past experience with chairing dissertation committees and directing candidates through the dissertation process; 2) proficiency in doctoral level courses especially in the area of qualitative and quantitative research. Special Requirements Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Sample Research Publication Sample Syllabi List of (3) References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
