    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/15824": {
      "title": "Counseling Clinical Faculty",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Counseling Clinical Faculty Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Counseling Clinical Faculty Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F250020P Open Date 10/01/2024 Close Date 01/17/2025 Faculty Rank Lecturer Title Counseling Clinical Faculty Salary $64,000 to $66,000 Annual Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Job Description Summary Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Teach master’s level counseling students across a CACREP accredited curriculum including supervise practicum/internship students. Required Education PhD, EdD, Psy D in Counselor Education & Supervision, Counseling Psychology, Or Related Field. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of and content expertise/competency in counseling diverse populations Strong critical thinking and problem-solving acumen. Ability to proactively identify challenges and barriers to stated objective and employ assistance in addressing these. Demonstration of Emotional Intelligence and professional maturity. Research experience and abilities. Strong communication acumen including written, oral, and listening. Ability to collaborate and work as part of a team Preferred Qualifications Independent Licensure required. Minimum one year experience teaching at The Graduate Level, preferably in a CACREP program. Experience working with diverse Populations Special Requirements Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Do you agree to a criminal background check? Yes No How many years of work experience do you have in Higher Education? 0 - less than 1 year 1 - 3 years 4 - 6 years 7 - 10 years Over 10 years How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Indeed Linkedin HigherEd Jobs CSU Website Personal referral Website Advertisement/Publication Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae References Transcripts Teaching Philosophy Letters of Reference Optional Documents Sample Research Publication If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Empl